"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[5808],{25808:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"kurs-dollara-nizhe-83-rubley-nalogovyy-period-oktyabr-2026","locale":"en","title":"Dollar falls below 83 rubles for the first time since August despite the largest currency purchases since 2022","description":"The official dollar rate for October 20 is 82.85 rubles, its lowest since August. Why the ruble is strengthening ahead of October 28 taxes despite Finance Ministry currency purchases.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Bank of Russia set the official dollar rate for October 20 at 82.85 rubles, 77 kopecks below the previous rate. It had not been below 83 since August 22. The euro fell to 93.23 rubles and the yuan to 12.39. On the over-the-counter market, the dollar touched 82.56 rubles on October 19. Early in the month, the situation was the opposite: the official rate rose to 85.71 rubles on October 7. Over 2 weeks, the ruble recovered that loss."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"The October 7 weakening was attributed to currency purchases under the fiscal rule. The Finance Ministry saves windfall revenues from expensive oil in the National Wealth Fund by buying currency and gold. It is spending 279.42 billion rubles on this from October 7 to November 6. Including Bank of Russia sales, the state is buying 12.1 billion rubles per day. That is 6 times September\'s amount and the largest volume since January 2022."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Imagine a freelancer paid in dollars who must pay rent in rubles by the 28th. They hold dollars throughout the first half of the month, then sell a large amount a week before the deadline. Exporters operate similarly. September taxes are due on October 28. October oil and gas budget revenue is estimated at about 1 trillion rubles, 0.5 trillion more than September. Much of the difference is the quarterly additional-income tax, about 0.36 trillion. That is why the second half of the month is called the tax-payment period on the exchange."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Analysts estimate October currency sales by the largest exporters at about $4 billion. At the current exchange rate, monthly state purchases are about $3.2 billion, spread evenly over 22 trading days. As a result, currency supply exceeds demand toward month-end. External factors also helped the ruble. On October 19, the dollar index against major currencies fell by 1.2% from its recent high, while the US postponed tariffs on buyers of Russian oil."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For people paying for imported goods, travel and international transfers, the current exchange rate is better than 2 weeks ago. Shop prices respond with a lag because sellers purchase goods in advance. The 14% key rate also supports the ruble: loans are expensive, import demand is restrained, and ruble deposits yield more than foreign-currency ones. A strong ruble is unfavorable for exporters and the budget because each barrel sold for foreign currency brings fewer rubles."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Vladimir Evstifeev of Zenit Bank expects the dollar could fall toward 82 rubles by October 28. After the tax deadline, exporters need fewer rubles and their sales usually subside, whereas Finance Ministry purchases continue until November 6. The ministry will announce a new purchase volume in early November, depending on October\'s oil price. Expensive oil means large November purchases too. Cheaper oil would reduce both state purchases and exporters\' revenue."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did the dollar fall below 83 rubles in October 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Oil companies pay September taxes by October 28, and October oil and gas budget revenue is estimated at about 1 trillion rubles, twice September\'s amount. Exporters sell currency to pay. Supply exceeded state purchases under the fiscal rule, strengthening the ruble."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Why is the ruble strengthening if the Finance Ministry is buying currency?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"The state buys currency in equal daily portions of about 12 billion rubles. Exporters sell unevenly, most heavily before the tax deadline. Sellers outnumber buyers in the second half of the month."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"What will happen to the exchange rate after October 28?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"After paying taxes, exporters need fewer rubles and usually reduce currency sales. Finance Ministry purchases at their current volume will continue until November 6; the next volume depends on October\'s oil price."}],"sources":[{"label":"Dollar falls below 83 rubles for the first time in two months","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9042314"},{"label":"Dollar approaches 82.5 rubles","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9042203"},{"label":"Central bank lowers the dollar exchange rate","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/19/tsb-ponizil-kurs-dollara"},{"label":"Bank of Russia reduces the dollar rate by 77 kopecks","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/finance/news/2026/10/19/1238342-kurs-dollara"},{"label":"US dollar exchange rate for October 8, 2026","url":"https://ppt.ru/currencies/usd/08-10-2026"},{"label":"Russian oil and gas budget revenue to reach 1 trillion rubles in October","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/15/neftegazovye-dokhody-byudzheta-rf-vyrastut-na-10-v-oktyabre-2625gg-do-1-trln-rub-raschyot-reyter-a208727"},{"label":"Ruble continues rising with oil-price and tax-payment support","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/19/rubl-prodolzhaet-rost-s-uchetom-neftyanoy-i-nalogovoy-podderzhki-geopolitiki-a208952"},{"label":"Finance Ministry to buy currency and gold worth 279.42 billion rubles from October 7 to November 6","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9006327"}],"sourceBodySha256":"f25608d7c3546bcf7841b9396fc0c3e8ef4ad41fa20f369f655ea9a55be665d4"}')}}]);